<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isparta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isparta is a city in the Lakes Region of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, capital of the province of the same name. In the 14th century it was one of the main towns of the Hamidid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> principality that ruled the lake district, before passing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. It is known for growing roses and producing rose oil, and for its carpets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isparta.jpg" alt="Isparta" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isparta at Turkish Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DaglardanIsparta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
